## Non-Eliminable Risks

> These risks exist but cannot be fully eliminated. The user has been informed and must decide to proceed.

| Risk | Details | Impact | User Decision |
|------|---------|--------|---------------|
| Transitive dependencies | Libraries your libraries use may contain undiscovered CVEs | Medium | Monitor with Dependabot or Renovate |
| Supply chain attacks | Any package registry entry can be hijacked by a compromised maintainer | Low–Medium | Pin exact versions, use lockfiles (package-lock.json / poetry.lock) |
| Zero-day vulnerabilities | Unknown CVEs may exist in any audited library | Low (statistically) | Accept as residual risk; monitor CVE feeds |
| Unaudited indirect deps | Only direct dependencies are audited by default | Low–Medium | Run `npm audit` / `pip-audit` regularly to catch transitive issues |
